mente 1 por cada 2,000 a 2,500 recién nacidas vivas. Además, el Síndrome de Turner puede estar asociado con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar enfermedades como la enfermedad celíaca. Es importante destacar que esta condición puede requerir tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento (GH) para abordar algunas de sus complicaciones.", "SÍNDROME DE PRADER-WILLI:Sindrome de Prader-Willi is a genetic disorder that affects growth and is also an approved indication for GH treatment.", "SÍNDROME DE NOONAN:Sindrome de Noonan is a genetic disorder that can cause growth issues, but is not approved for GH treatment in Spain.", "TALLA BAJA IDIOPÁTICA:Talla baja idiopática is a condition of short stature with no known cause, which is treated with GH in the United States but not in Spain.", "GEN SHOX:El gen SHOX está relacionado con el crecimiento y su alteración puede causar deficiencia de crecimiento, lo que puede ser tratado con GH.", "MICRO-ADENOMAS:Micro-adenomas are small tumors of the pituitary gland that can affect hormone production, relevant in the context of Cushing's disease.", "MACRO-ADENOMAS:Macro-adenomas are larger tumors of the pituitary gland that can lead to excessive hormone production, significant in the context of Cushing's disease.", "HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO:The \"HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO,\" or Growth Hormone, is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration. It is utilized in various medical treatments, particularly for patients with growth deficiencies. In the context of critical care, growth hormone is mentioned as a potential treatment option for patients, including pediatric patients with extensive burns, to aid in their recovery. \n\nResearch indicates that growth hormone can enhance magnesium absorption in the body. Additionally, while growth hormone treatment has been shown to increase muscle mass, the results regarding strength improvements have been inconsistent across different clinical trials. Overall, growth hormone is a significant therapeutic agent in both pediatric and critical care settings, aimed at promoting recovery and addressing growth-related issues.", "ARTRALGIAS:Artralgias (Joint pain) are a common side effect associated with growth hormone treatment.", "GINECOMASTIA:Ginecomastia, also known as gynecomastia, is a medical condition characterized by the enlargement of breast tissue in males. This condition can arise due to various factors, including hormonal imbalances, and is often noted as a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment. Ginecomastia can occur in individuals with specific genetic conditions, such as Klinefelter syndrome and Wilson's disease, where hormonal imbalances are prevalent. Additionally, it can manifest during puberty as a natural developmental change. The condition may also be a side effect of testosterone therapy, leading to an increase in breast tissue. Overall, ginecomastia is a multifaceted condition that can result from a variety of hormonal influences and medical treatments.", "HIPERTENSIÓN INTRACRANEAL BENIGNA:Hipertensión intracraneal benigna (Benign Intracranial Hypertension) is a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment that can lead to increased pressure in the skull.", "NEVUS:Nevus (Mole) refers to a pigmented skin lesion that may increase in number, size, and pigmentation as a side effect of growth hormone treatment.)<|COMPLETE|>", "PEINÓ R.:Peinó R. is the author of the \"Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición,\" a comprehensive work that addresses growth hormone deficiency and its treatment. The manual covers this condition in both children and adults, providing valuable insights into its implications and management across different age groups.", "GH RECOMBINANTE:GH recombinante refers to the recombinant growth hormone used in medical treatments, which can have various side effects."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 